    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "Wapping Hydraulic Power Station Open Days",
            "paragraphs": [
                "A chance to get inside the historic Wapping Hydraulic Power Station, a prime example of London’s industrial heritage which has been closed for the last decade. This is an opportunity to see the engine room and boiler house of what was the world's last hydraulic power station to be decommissioned.",
                "This event is organised by Glass Castle Foundation, which is bringing Wapping Hydraulic Power Station back to life as a venue for experimental artistic practice."
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "What to expect",
            "paragraphs": [
                "There will be a drop-in drawing workshop hosted by architects from ByOthers, Glass Castle's design consultant. Participants are invited to explore the building’s distinctive textures by making graphite rubbings or clay tile stamping, which when assembled will form a collective texture map.",
                "We will also be joined by members of the History of Wapping Trust who can share their expertise, maps and publications about the history of the area.\n \nThere will also be opportunities to join short informal tours with Open House guides, or simply walk around the building at your own leisure."
            ]
        }
    ],
